"""Long-form article — Best Rooftop Cargo Boxes for 2020–2025 Hyundai Palisade (1st gen, LX2).
Mirrors the approved F-150 tonneau pilot. No invented hands-on testing: box specs come from Yakima, Thule,
Rhino-Rack, INNO (via etrailer) and Rightline Gear (via RealTruck) pages fetched 2026-09-27; vehicle facts from
db/migrations/003_vehicles.sql and the Palisade roof-rack article (flush rails, Thule kit 6008, 50 in bars, 165 lb,
~32 in spread). Hyundai accessory crossbar 220 lb figure is from the Hyundai installation guide as quoted by owners on
palisadeforums.org; hatch clearance (about 71 in) from an etrailer expert answer.
Source fixes 2026-10-04 (round 2): roof figure now cites Hyundai's 2020, 2023 and 2024 specification sheets (roof rails load capacity 220 lb; sheets do not say whether it is for driving only) alongside the forum-quoted 220 lb accessory crossbar figure, with "the lowest number applies"; the 163 lb Motion 3 XXL remainder restated as crossbars plus gear under the roof figure; factory receiver wording removed (the sheets list no tow hitch); rails worded as the trims the listings name; etrailer hatch clearance worded as "gives" not "measured"; Telluride line reduced to "related" (Wikipedia).
"""

