FAQ = [
 ("What size cargo box fits a 2020–2025 Hyundai Palisade?",
  "The Palisade's roof and hatch leave room for almost any size. An etrailer expert puts its rear hatch clearance at about 71 in, well past the 55 in a Thule Motion XT needs, so even the 91.3 in Thule Motion 3 XXL (21 cu ft) is a realistic choice. For most families a 16 cu ft box like the Yakima SkyBox 16 is the sweet spot: enough for third-row luggage while leaving weight for gear under a 165 lb bar rating."),
 ("How much weight can the Palisade's roof crossbars hold?",
  "It depends on the bars, and the roof has its own figure. Hyundai's 2020, 2023 and 2024 Palisade specification sheets print a roof rails load capacity of 220 lb. The sheets do not say whether that is for driving only. Thule rates its Evo Flush Rail system for the Palisade at 165 lb, which is the system's rating. Palisade owners also quote Hyundai's accessory crossbar installation guide: 220 lb (100 kg), evenly distributed, for the set. The lowest number applies. The bars, the box and everything in it count toward the roof figure."),
 ("What crossbar spread does the Palisade allow for a cargo box?",
  "In an etrailer answer about a Thule Motion XT, the expert gives the Palisade's crossbar spread as about 32 in. That sits inside the range of every box here with a published spread: 24 to 34.5 in for the SkyBox 16, 21-13/16 to 36-9/16 in for the Thule Motion 3, 24 to 39 in for the INNO Wedge 660 and 620 to 930 mm (about 24.4 to 36.6 in) for the Rhino-Rack MasterFit 440. The DeepSpace 10 needs 32 to 46 in, so 32 in is right at its minimum."),
 ("Will a roof box hit the Palisade's liftgate?",
  "Rarely, if it is mounted forward. The etrailer expert gives about 71 in of rear hatch clearance on the Palisade against 55 in needed for a Thule Motion XT. Thule lists more than 54 13/16 in of front clearance for the Motion 3 XXL, the longest box here. Measure your own Palisade from the front crossbar to the line where the roof meets the hatch, and open the power liftgate slowly the first time."),
 ("Do I need Thule or Hyundai crossbars for a cargo box?",
  "No particular brand, but they must be flush-rail bars that name the 2020–2025 Palisade. Hyundai sells accessory crossbars (220 lb per its install guide, as owners quote it), Thule fits it with Evo Flush Rail feet, kit 6008 and 50 in WingBar Evo bars (165 lb), and Amazon sets clamp to the same rails. A box clamps to any of them. Raised-rail towers won't grip the Palisade's flush rails. See our Palisade roof rack page for fit-checked bars."),
 ("Will a 2020–2025 Palisade cargo box fit the 2026 Palisade?",
  "The box will, because boxes clamp to crossbars, not the car. The 2026 Palisade is a new generation with a different body, so buy crossbars listed for 2026 and re-check the spread, hatch clearance and roof figure in its manual. Your 2020–2025 bars shouldn't be assumed to fit."),
 ("Can I carry a cargo box and bikes on a Palisade?",
  "Yes, with a narrow box. Thule's Palisade bars are 50 in long. A full-width box like the 36 in SkyBox 16 leaves about 14 in, which is tight for a bike mount; the 26.5 in Yakima SkyBox NX Skinny leaves about 23.5 in. Add up the box, the bike mount, the bike and the cargo, and keep it under your bar rating, 165 lb on the Thule system, and never above the 220 lb roof rails figure on Hyundai's spec sheets."),
 ("Can I open the Palisade's sunroof with a cargo box on?",
  "Check it parked before you rely on it. Flush-rail feet hold the bars a few inches above the roof, and a box's front edge can sit close to the sunroof opening. For other SUVs, etrailer's experts advise against opening a sunroof or panoramic roof while a box is installed, because the glass can make contact with the rack or box. Keep it closed on the road."),
 ("Will a cargo box fit in my garage on a Palisade?",
  "Measure first. The boxes here add 11 in (INNO Wedge 660), 15 in (SkyBox 16), 16 in (NX Skinny, DeepSpace 10), 17 in (Rhino-Rack MasterFit 440), about 18 in (Motion 3 XXL, Rightline Sport 3) on top of the crossbars, which already sit above the flush rails. Measure the Palisade with bars fitted, add the box height, and compare it with the garage door opening."),
 ("Is a roof box or a hitch cargo carrier better on a Palisade?",
  "Hyundai's 2020, 2023 and 2024 specification sheets rate the Palisade at 5,000 lb with trailer brakes and list no tow hitch as equipment, so a receiver is something a dealer or an owner adds. Look under the rear bumper. With a receiver fitted, a hitch carrier suits heavy items like coolers and water jugs without touching the roof figure. A roof box is better for soft, bulky luggage, keeps the liftgate and camera clear, and locks. For an eight-seat Palisade that is full to the third row, many families use both."),
]

